ctly one disease name functions pre-nominally before a non-disease head noun, with no coordinated disease referent in the span.\n  - **Negative constraint:** Do NOT apply this rule when the coordinated elements are not disease names or disease-site specifiers (e.g., coordinated drugs, anatomical structures, symptoms, or procedures), when the coordinator belongs to a single fixed disease-name unit that denotes one disease entity, or when the coordinated items are aliases for the same disease. In those cases, the single-disease classification applies. A surrounding frame such as \"family history of\" or \"risk of\" must not determine the label on its own.\n  - **Generalization:** The trigger is the structural presence of two distinct disease referents bound by a coordinator under a shared head, not any specific lexical item (e.g., \"breast,\" \"ovarian,\" \"cancer\") or any particular frame. The rule applies to any coordinator and any disease-type or disease-site pairing.\n  - **Consistency:** This keeps CompositeMention for multi-disease spans, Modifier for single-disease attributive uses, and SpecificDisease for standalone disease names, matching the entity definitions.", "type": "text"}], "diagnostics": null, "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 1587, "output_tokens": 2678, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 2134}, "service_tier": "batch", "speed": "standard"}}}